{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 4 and 5 where prices fell from ~89 to ~77); forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 10-20 points in the first half of the horizon.",
    "Forecasts display significant mean reversion lag; they predict slow, linear recovery after a crash (e.g., Example 4), whereas true outcomes show explosive V-shaped rebounds within 5-7 days.",
    "Sentiment history is largely irrelevant to short-term price direction in these episodes; low sentiment scores do not prevent sharp rallies once the downtrend reverses.",
    "Apply a negative correction factor of -10 to -15 points to the first 10 forecast steps when the last 3 days of history show a decline of >10%.",
    "Switch from linear extrapolation to exponential growth logic for the final 10-15 forecast steps if the true outcome shows volatility spikes exceeding 5% in any single day."
  ]
}
